60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: The candidates are here! I’m already leaning toward the textiles, since local pieces mean no scary transport bills.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: @Mio, local is sensible, but who will run the demonstrations? My staffing report shows we have no spare hands for that.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: @Mio, your local bias ignores the data. The comment slips explicitly demand live presence, which the textiles offer, but the head counts favor motion.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Mio, the textiles are light, but the structural survey is irrelevant if the room is empty. I need to know if the floor can bear the demonstration tables.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Mio, local is wise. No distant lenders means no cut-off disasters. I can finally sleep at night knowing the delivery is safe.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Victoria, the craftspeople come with the show! They bring their own tools, so we just need a safe, sturdy table.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: @Mio, that assumes the craftspeople are reliable. My roster shows no backup if they cancel. Who stands in the room then?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: @Victoria, the data shows presence drives return visits. If the craftspeople cancel, the room is empty, and the audience leaves.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Mio, demonstration tables are light. The floor will bear them easily. My concern is the rigging for the light show, not your looms.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Asuka, you are right. The light show’s rigging is the true danger. I fear the paperwork for those distant studios will slip again.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Shion, but the comment slips say people come back for the people, not the machines! The textiles give us that human touch.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: @Mio, the craftspeople are the risk. If they cancel, we have no backup. The light show is safer, even if it is heavier.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: @Victoria, you are wrong. The head counts prove motion wins. The light show is the only candidate that satisfies the data.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Shion, the light show requires overhead rigging. The suspended bay cannot bear it. It is physically impossible.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Asuka, if the bay cannot hold the rigging, the light show is dead on arrival. The textiles remain our only safe path.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Shion, I hear you, but the light show is physically impossible! The textiles are the only one that fits our budget, staff, and building.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: @Mio, I concede the structural point. The light show is impossible. I vote for the textiles, accepting the staffing risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: @Asuka, the physics override my data. I concede. The textiles are the only viable option. I vote for them.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Shion, the structure is the final word. I vote for the textiles. They respect the building's limits.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Mio, I am with you. The textiles are safe, local, and kind to our schedule. I vote for them.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
